  "body": "While trying to merge https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/f99550b642df864e8bd1b18d91e366647df751bc?diff=unified into https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6315 I noticed the following potential issues:\r\n\r\n- I think navigationParams's uncommited preloads can end up null by the time we reach https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#initialise-the-document-object step 18, causing us to iterate over null. Probably we should guard it with a null check, or always use the empty list instead of null?\r\n\r\n- In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigation-params-uncommitted-preloads `document` should be `Document`.\r\n\r\n- `<embed>` and `<object>` ignore early hints, since the \"if resource is a response\" case in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate always sets uncommited preloads to null, instead of extracting them from the response. Is this desired? Does this match implementations? (If this is not the desired behavior, and we want to do the full redirect following logic for embed and object, it's going to be a big pain to spec... maybe best to just leave an XXX box.)\r\n\r\n- PDFs and error pages due to, e.g., CSP blockage, ignore early hints, because https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#read-ua-inline creates a navigation params with no uncommited preloads. Is this desired? Do we have tests? (Maybe the answer is different for PDFs vs. error pages?)",
